FLT, Felix Terminal for MS-DOS (DJGPP, 32-bit, needs DPMI: vmdos's own), in
C:\VMDOS\NET on C: only (the boot floppy has no room).

  FLT.EXE   github.com/jasonbrianhall/felixterminal, msdos/ (prebuilt,
            unmodified; `make` there, `make dist` for FLT.EXE and README.TXT)

Felix Terminal's terminal, its sixel and kitty graphics and its built-in SSH
client (libssh2), drawn on a VESA mode: SSH from DOS to a Linux box and run
timg, img2sixel, gnuplot's sixel terminal and the like, with the pictures on
the DOS screen. It uses vmdos's own TCP (the same socket layer as SSH, WGET
and LYNX), IPv4 and IPv6.

    STARTNET                       (once: the TCP/IP settings, by DHCP)
    FLT user@host                  (or FLT host, FLT user@host:2222)
    FLT -g 1280x800 user@host      (another screen mode)

    FLT [-4|-6] [-p port] [-l user] [-i keyfile] [-g WxH[xBITS]] [-f size]
        [-t theme] [user@]host[:port] [command]

  -g WxH[xBITS]  the VESA mode (or SET FLT_VIDEO=WxH). Default 1024x768,
                 32-bit if there is one, else 16-bit; otherwise the largest
                 mode of 640x480 or more.
  -f size        font size in pixels (16: 10x22 cells, 102x34 characters at
                 1024x768). DejaVu Sans Mono, built in.
  -i keyfile     the private key. Otherwise ~/.ssh/config's IdentityFile, then
                 ~/.ssh/id_ed25519, id_rsa, ... ~ is %HOME%, C:\HOME if not set
                 (as vmdos's SSH); known_hosts is there too.
  -4 / -6        IPv4 or IPv6 only. Otherwise IPv6 first only if this PC has a
                 global address.
  -t theme       a theme by name (or its start) or number (or SET FLT_THEME=).

Keys and mouse (a DOS mouse driver: CTMOUSE, or vmdos's):

  Shift+PgUp/PgDn/Home/End   scroll back (images too); any other key returns
  Left-drag                  select; copies on release
  Middle-click, Shift+Ins    paste (FLT's own clipboard; bracketed paste)
  Shift+mouse                select even when a program (vim mouse=a, htop,
                             mc) has asked for the mouse
  Right-click                menu: Copy, Paste, Themes, Resolution (lists the
                             VESA modes and switches at once); Esc closes it

The theme and mode chosen are kept in %HOME%\FLT.CFG (theme=, mode=WxHxBITS);
-g/FLT_VIDEO and -t/FLT_THEME override it. SET FLT_LOG=file writes a debug log.
TERM is xterm-256color; timg -pk draws with kitty graphics, timg -ps with sixel.

Not in the DOS build: OpenGL effects, sound, SFTP, port forwarding, X11
forwarding, the SSH key manager, telnet, serial, a local shell and the
system clipboard.
